From ced770c1f1930f6f3e63fb705521fd618303f466 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <ben@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 14:37:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libfprint: Add driver for EgisTec EH576 fingerprint sensor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a libfprint FpImageDevice driver for the LighTuning/EgisTec EH576
optical fingerprint sensor (USB ID 1c7a:0576), found in several Lenovo
ThinkPad laptop models.

The sensor captures 68×52 pixel frames at 500 DPI (~3.5×2.6 mm active
area). Key implementation details:

- Protocol: fixed register-write + capture sequence over bulk USB,
  with EGIS/SIGE 4-byte command framing (reverse-engineered from
  Windows driver USB captures)

- Image pipeline:
  1. Crop active 68×52 columns from 103-byte USB stride
  2. Normalize dynamic range (max-stretch to 0–255)
  3. Unsharp mask (5-tap box blur, strength 1.5×) for ridge contrast
  4. 2× bilinear upscale → 136×104 px at 1000 DPI
  5. Mirror-pad by 24 px on all sides → 184×152 px

- Mirror padding (the key fix): NBIS marks direction-map blocks at
  the image border INVALID because its 24-px DFT window extends into
  uniform constant padding. This causes remove_near_invblock_V2() to
  remove every ridge endpoint touching the image boundary, leaving
  only 1–2 interior minutiae — too few for bozorth3. Reflecting 24 px
  of real fingerprint content on all four sides gives those border
  blocks valid DFT ridge directions, yielding 12–25 minutiae per
  capture and reliable bozorth3 matching.

- 7 enrollment stages to cope with the small active area
- bozorth3 threshold of 10 (genuine matches score 15–29;
  adjacent fingers score ≤8; unrelated fingers score 0)

Also adds two fp_dbg() lines to fp-image.c (image size/ppmm and
minutiae count) that are useful for all image-device drivers.

Signed-off-by: Ben <ben@localhost>
